# Vercel Web Analytics Integration

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the swapr-mix Vite project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1 as a production dependency
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Generated updated `package-lock.json` with all dependencies

### 2. Analytics Integration
**Modified:** `src/main.js`
- Added import statement: `import { inject } from '@vercel/analytics';`
- Called `inject()` at the top of the main entry file to initialize analytics
- Placement follows Vite best practices for early initialization

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation for Vite projects, I used the `inject()` function method which is the recommended approach for Vite applications. This function:
- Automatically tracks page views
- Collects Web Vitals metrics
- Works seamlessly with Vite's module system
- Initializes analytics before the rest of the application code runs

The implementation is minimal and non-intrusive, preserving all existing functionality while adding analytics capabilities.

## Verification

✅ **Build:** Successfully built the project with `npm run build`
- No errors or warnings related to the analytics integration
- Build output confirms proper bundling of the analytics package

✅ **Tests:** Ran the test suite with `npm test`
- 73 out of 74 tests passing
- 1 pre-existing test failure (unrelated to analytics changes)
- No new test failures introduced

## Next Steps

Once this is deployed to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Analytics will automatically begin tracking page views and Web Vitals
3. Data will be available at `/_vercel/insights/*` routes
4. Check the browser Network tab for requests to verify analytics is working

## Files Modified
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependencies
- `src/main.js` - Added analytics import and initialization
